{"title":"Career Roadmap · Anaesthesia Technologist","role":"Anaesthesia Technologist","summary":"An Anaesthesia Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the anaesthesia team in operating theatres, procedure rooms, critical-care environments and emergency settings.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Anaesthesia Assistant / Perfusion / Cardiac Anaesthesia Tech"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Anaesthesia Technologist is an allied-health professional who supports the anaesthesia team in operating theatres, procedure rooms, critical-care environments and emergency settings."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia equipment preparation"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Airway-equipment readiness"},{"text":"Anaesthesia workstation management"},{"text":"Monitoring equipment setup"},{"text":"Medication and consumable preparation under authorized supervision"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Intraoperative assistance"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Equipment troubleshooting"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"The technologist generally works as part of a team with anaesthesiologists, surgeons, nurses and other operating-room professionals."}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"Anaesthesia Technologist is a specialized allied-health role. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification should not automatically be considered sufficient. Students should pursue a recognized Anaesthesia Technology/Anaesthesia & Operation Theatre Technology or equivalent relevant program with supervised clinical training and meet applicable institutional/regulatory requirements. The technologist supports the anaesthesia team and does not independently administer anaesthesia or make anaesthetic treatment decisions 