reness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Airway"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airway equipment preparation"},{"text":"Difficult-airway equipment awareness"},{"text":"Suction"},{"text":"Ventilation equipment"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"BP"},{"text":"EtCO₂"},{"text":"Temperature"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"PACU workflow"},{"text":"Infection control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia workstation"},{"text":"Patient monitors"},{"text":"EMR"},{"text":"Anaesthesia information systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Team communication"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Equipment readiness"},{"text":"Rapid escalation"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia Technology Foundation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Anaesthesia Equipment"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Airway Equipment"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Patient Monitoring"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Ventilation Fundamentals"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Anaesthesia Pharmacology Awareness"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Emergency & Critical Care"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Operating Theatre Workflow"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Infection Control"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Cardiac Anaesthesia Exposure"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"PACU / Recovery"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"EMR / Anaesthesia Information Systems"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Medical Equipment Management"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"BLS / Emergency Preparedness"}]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Anaesthesia Technology Qualification","Clinical Internship","OT & Anaesthesia Exposure","Anaesthesia Technologist","Advanced Airway/Critical-Care Experience","Senior Anaesthesia Technologist","Cardiac/Neuro/Pediatric Specialist or OT Coordinator","Clinical Applications/Management"]},{"type":"p","text":"For maximum employability, combine anaesthesia equipment expertise + airway support + patient monitoring + ventilation fundamentals + emergency preparedness + infection control + OT workflow + cardiac/critical-care exposure + digital anaesthesia systems."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-fitment mapping note","text":"This target should be mapped primarily to students pursuing a recognized Anaesthesia Technology or equivalent relevant allied-health program with supervised clinical training. “Anaesthesia Assistant,” “Perfusion Technologist,” and “Anaesthesia Technologist” should remain separate career pathways in the database because their education, technical scope and clinical responsibilities differ. An Anaesthesia Technologist supports the anaesthesia team and does not independently diagnose, prescribe or administer anaesthesia outside their authorized scope."}]}]}